From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:41:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock A18 Pro VideoDecoder with native synthetic
 frames

Expose secure-Window and DedicatedWorker VideoDecoder, EncodedVideoChunk,
VideoFrame and VideoColorSpace through native bindings. Keep SharedWorker
and ServiceWorker exposure absent and preserve resource-loading defaults.

Advertise a conservative synthetic H.264 avc1/avc3 baseline/main/extended/
high capability through isConfigSupported, including the benchmark's
avc1.640028 1920x1080 prefer-hardware query. Clone recognized configuration
and description values, reject malformed configurations and report valid
unsupported codecs/configurations as unsupported. This is a persona policy,
not a measurement of host hardware or an exhaustive Apple codec inventory.

Model the decoder's constructor, callbacks, EventTarget surface, configured/
unconfigured/closed state, decodeQueueSize, dequeue events, FIFO synthetic
output, flush, reset and close. Snapshot metadata per queued chunk, require
a key after configuration/reset/flush, reject pending flushes on reset or
close, and asynchronously close unsupported configurations via the error
callback. Apply display aspect ratios by increasing presentation dimensions.

Produce one opaque-black RGBA VideoFrame per accepted nonempty chunk with
its timestamp and duration. Support frame metadata, crop/stride-aware
allocationSize/copyTo, independent clone/close, and RGBA-buffer/frame
constructors. EncodedVideoChunk owns a copy of input bytes and supports
copyTo. VideoColorSpace provides readonly metadata and toJSON.

Reuse existing JS-owned callback/listener storage and dispatch helpers.
Tasks retain wrappers while pending, events retain their decoder target
through a private JS edge, callback storage uses own data properties, and
buffer bytes are resolved after potentially reentrant argument conversion.
Detach decoders before context scheduler teardown. No new unit tests.

Scope: API mock only. No compressed-bitstream parsing, real H.264 decoding,
GPU operations, host codec probing, VideoEncoder/AudioDecoder, or WebRTC.
Decoded pixels are always synthetic. Frame pixel handling is RGBA only;
other pixel formats, media-element/canvas source constructors, transfer/
structured-clone semantics, exact WebIDL numeric coercion and full browser
codec/colorimetry behavior are not implemented. Detached empty chunk/config
buffers currently follow the existing BufferSource conversion (empty bytes).
Keep benchmark assertions unchanged and existing patches byte-for-byte.

Validation in development: existing upstream tests 1658/1658; temporary
CDP diagnostics 85/85, including lifecycle, raw bytes, synthetic pixels,
callbacks, GC survival, retained targets, reentrant detachment, unsupported
queued operations, dedicated-worker output, secure/insecure Window and
worker exposure, SharedWorker absence and navigation teardown. One reviewer
pass completed; all five reported findings addressed. Exported-stack build,
upstream suite and benchmark results are recorded in ignored .build artifacts.

References:
https://www.w3.org/TR/webcodecs/#videodecoder-interface
https://www.w3.org/TR/webcodecs/#videoframe-interface
https://www.w3.org/TR/webcodecs/#encodedvideochunk-interface
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
